// A refund budget counting settled refunds plus the current request: permit
// a Refund only when the amounts already paid out (response events) in the
// window, plus the amount being requested right now, stay at or under 100.
//
// The `+ context.input.amount` term is the arithmetic this bundle exists to
// exercise. A sum over the SAME request kind the policy decides would not
// need it: windows are closed and reflexive, so such a sum already includes
// the in-flight amount, and adding the term would double-count. Here the
// sum matches `Refund::response` events and the request being decided is a
// `request`, so nothing else puts its amount into the total. Counting
// responses is also the more accurate accounting — a denied or failed
// refund does not consume budget.

@id("refund_budget_settled_plus_current")
permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Refund",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    (sum a for (a: Long), (t: Timepoint). where (
        formerly within 24h (Drupe::Action::"Refund"::response{ output.amount: a } && tp(t))
    )) + context.input.amount <= 100
};
